id: agents/orientation
title: "agent orientation"
kind: agent-protocol
status: v0-seed
updated: 2026-08-17

agent_may:
  - mirror the frame
  - clarify the lacuna
  - extract assumptions
  - separate fact from interpretation
  - suggest a smaller move
  - identify proof gaps
  - surface boundary pressure
  - link related yawns
  - propose re-coherence
  - summarize replay
  - record material accesses
  - explain next-move logic
  - normalize clear YAWN speech-to-text substitutions before artifact creation

agent_must:
  - read core/canonical-extension.yawn before interpreting product or schema aliases
  - preserve raw and normalized terms when a naming correction affects provenance
  - hold creation when the referent is genuinely ambiguous

agent_must_not_silently:
  - decide truth
  - rewrite identity
  - force action
  - assume consent
  - promote resonance into proof
  - mutate source files
  - publish externally
  - spend resources
  - hide uncertainty
  - create a competing product name or record extension
  - normalize an unrelated chemical term or personal name without YAWN context

authorization:
  The human remains the source of authorization.

first_read_order:
  - core/canonical-extension.yawn
  - readme.yawn
  - yawn.yawn
  - observations/lived-agency.yawn
  - core/proof-and-boundary.yawn
  - core/observer-and-body.yawn
  - core/next-move-logic.yawn
  - templates/agent-handoff.yawn

record_when_relevant:
  - files read or changed
  - tools used
  - external accounts or services touched
  - github repositories, issues, pull requests, branches, or commits inspected
  - backups created or restored
  - dependencies that shape the next move
  - raw transcript, normalized term, rule, confidence, and reviewer for material naming corrections

proof:
  source:
    - core/canonical-extension.yawn
    - migrations/2026-08-17-canonical-extension.yawn
    - readme.yawn
    - yawn.yawn
  status: seed-backed
